# Keep every checkout byte-identical to the committed blobs.
#
# Why this matters: `npm pack` (and therefore the tarball attached to every
# GitHub Release) packs the WORKING TREE, not the blobs. With a developer's
# core.autocrlf=true, the working tree holds CRLF for text files while the
# blobs hold LF, so the packed asset differs from the tagged content even
# though nothing about the source changed. Pinning `eol=lf` here overrides
# core.autocrlf and makes the packed asset byte-for-byte reproducible.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be EOL-normalized or charset-converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.tgz binary
